## Stub qualification ladder — one rung per step, never skip to the top

Precheck (read-only, one non-intrusive attach): SMU_AG0..AG11 alarm-clean
check (not clean -> record and STOP), SCU_RSTCON baseline read.

1. SCRATCH RAM: identify a safe, unused RAM region from the linker map
   (not touched by running firmware or DMA). Record the address. All stub
   staging happens there.
2. MECHANICS PROOF (harmless): stub = write a magic value to a scratch
   word, then endless loop. Stage it: Break (brief), download stub, set
   the core's PC to the stub, disable interrupts for that core (first stub
   instruction or ICR via debugger while halted), Go. Verify the magic
   value appeared, re-read AG0..11 (must still be clean), then Break and
   restore nothing - proceed only if clean. This rung proves: RAM
   download, PC hijack, execution, and that staging itself latches no
   alarm.
3. ENDINIT-CYCLE PROOF (still harmless): stub = Safety-ENDINIT unlock ->
   relock -> magic write -> loop. Transcribe the unlock sequence from the
   public iLLD source (IfxScuWdt_clearSafetyEndinit / setSafetyEndinit) -
   do not invent instruction sequences. Verify magic + AGs clean. This
   rung proves the password sequence works from the stub context.
4. LIVE INJECTION - application class FIRST (smaller reset domain), system
   class on a separate later run. Stub sequence: disable interrupts ->
   Safety-ENDINIT unlock -> SCU_RSTCON.SW = class -> Safety-ENDINIT
   relock -> CPU-ENDINIT unlock -> SCU_SWRSTCON.SWRSTREQ = 1 -> loop
   (never returns; the chip reboots). Execution: stage while briefly
   halted, Go, then IMMEDIATELY NoDebug so the reset happens with the
   debugger detached; wait the wake-up time; attach fresh (NoDebug then
   Attach); read stored cause + full register set.
   Acceptance: stored reset-cause CHANGES from baseline and decodes to the
   injected class; live RSTSTAT and all AG groups clear after boot; DUT
   answers over the normal channel; evidence CSV written. Record the stub
   bytes, load address, and the exact TRACE32 command log alongside.
5. If any rung fails or latches an alarm: STOP at that rung, record
   everything, do not improvise a variant in-session. A failed rung is the
   slot outcome.

## Safety rails

- One non-resetting attach per step; on failure run the probe-health check
  and STOP. No SYStem.Up, no SYStem.Mode Down, no retry storms.
- No debugger writes to SCU/SMU kernel space. RAM staging writes and
  stub-executed writes only.
- Never clear an alarm or reset-status register before it is recorded.
- No core may be left halted at any moment a reset can fire.
- Keep staging halts brief; re-verify AG cleanliness between rungs.
- Leave the DUT in Standby and the probe detached (NoDebug) at the end.
- Anything unexpected: stop, record, report - do not improvise.

